   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1c7a0e65",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Analying the internal representation drift using CKA and PWCCA(https://arxiv.org/pdf/1905.00414 and https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.05759)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b4c3afc4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## CKA\n",
    "### Step 1: Environment Setup\n",
    "First, we install the open-source `torch_cka` library. This library automatically handles the forward hooks, feature extraction, and matrix math required to generate a complete layer-by-layer similarity heatmap."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1d5be243",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "import torch.nn as nn\n",
    "from torch.utils.data import DataLoader, Dataset, Subset, TensorDataset\n",
    "from torchvision import datasets\n",
    "from torchvision.transforms import v2\n",
    "from torch_cka import CKA\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "020b6db0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 2: Handling the Resolution Mismatch\n",
    "Because the baseline model was trained on **300x200** images and the fine-tuned model expects **320x180** screen layouts, we cannot pass the exact same tensor to both. \n",
    "\n",
    "Instead, we will create **two separate DataLoaders** pointing to the exact same probe dataset, but applying their respective resizing transforms. `torch_cka` will pass `dataloader_natural` to Model 1 and `dataloader_screen` to Model 2, ensuring each model receives the resolution it is mathematically optimized for."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2d9cc5f0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Preparation of the Enrico dataset**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a66edc70",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "caltech_base_dataset = datasets.Caltech101(root=\"./data\", download=True)\n",
    "caltech_train_raw, _, _ = stratified_three_way_split(\n",
    "    dataset=caltech_base_dataset,\n",
    "    train_ratio=0.8,\n",
    "    val_ratio=0.1,\n",
    "    test_ratio=0.1\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "caltech_preprocess = make_caltech_base_transform(resize=(300, 200))\n",
    "caltech_train_raw_loader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader(\n",
    "    AugmentationWrapper(caltech_train_raw, caltech_preprocess),\n",
    "    batch_size=64,\n",
    "    shuffle=False,\n",
    "    num_workers=3\n",
    ")\n",
    "caltech_train_mean, caltech_train_std = mean_and_std_for_normalization(caltech_train_raw_loader)\n",
    "\n",
    "universal_base_nat_images = v2.Compose([\n",
    "    caltech_preprocess,\n",
    "    v2.Normalize(mean=caltech_train_mean, std=caltech_train_std, inplace=False)\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "universal_base_screen = v2.Compose([\n",
    "    screen_preprocess,\n",
    "    v2.Normalize(mean=screen_train_mean, std=screen_train_std, inplace=False)\n",
    "])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e8d97780",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "_, _, full_natural_test = CustomEnricoDataset.create_splits(\n",
    "    root=ENRICO_ROOT,\n",
    "    val_size=0.1,\n",
    "    test_size=0.1,\n",
    "    use_wireframes=False,\n",
    "    train_transform=universal_base_nat_images,\n",
    "    eval_transform=universal_base_nat_images\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "_, _, full_screen_test = CustomEnricoDataset.create_splits(\n",
    "    root=ENRICO_ROOT,\n",
    "    val_size=0.1,\n",
    "    test_size=0.1,\n",
